diagnosis_text:
Affected component: the Layer-3 gateway interface for Campus 2 VLAN 5 on sshswitch (Linux bridge br_v5 providing 10.5.0.254/24). Mechanism: VLAN 5 hosts (10.5.0.0/24) can switch locally on switch4 so intra-subnet pings work, but their default gateway 10.5.0.254 does not respond. From pc1, ping to 10.5.0.254 is 100% loss despite a valid default route via 10.5.0.254. On sshswitch, the SVI/bridge for VLAN 5 is present with IP 10.5.0.254/24, but the bridge itself is administratively down, so it neither bridges nor ARPs, making the gateway unreachable while same-subnet traffic remains unaffected. Localization: sshswitch shows br_v5 in DOWN state while the equivalent VLAN 6 bridge (br_v6 at 10.6.0.254/24) is UP and operating, matching the report that VLAN 6 users are unaffected. Evidence: ip a on sshswitch shows “8: br_v5 … state DOWN … inet 10.5.0.254/24”, whereas br_v6 is “state UP.” pc1 cannot ping 10.5.0.254, confirming gateway unreachability. Root cause: The VLAN 5 bridge interface br_v5 on sshswitch was left administratively down. Corrective fix: Bring up the gateway bridge and ensure it is enabled at boot: ip link set br_v5 up; verify member ports (eth0.5, bond0.5) remain enslaved; optionally restart the switch’s network service to persist. After br_v5 is UP, hosts in 10.5.0.0/24 should reach outside networks again. === END ===